\title{Arithmetisation}
\author{dhsorens}
\date{2026-08-18}
\meta{toc}{true}

\p{
    How a computation becomes algebra. Three formats dominate — [R1CS](dhsorens-002S),
    [Plonkish](dhsorens-002T), and [AIR](dhsorens-002U) — and [CCS](dhsorens-002V) is the claim that
    they are one object with different sparsity patterns.
}

\p{
    [Clean](dhsorens-002Y) sits at this layer: an embedded DSL that writes circuits for these
    formats in [Lean](dhsorens-lean), with the specification and the soundness proof next to the
    circuit. The open question is what "this circuit implements this specification" should mean, and
    which arithmetisation makes that statement easiest to prove — the same question as for [smart
    contract specifications](dhsorens-001J), with better-behaved mathematics.
}

